---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Polo Lounge",
  servesCuisine: ["American", "Italian"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-310-887-2777",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "9641 Sunset Blvd",
    addressLocality: "Beverly Hills",
    addressRegion: "CA",
    postalCode: "90210",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "The legendary dining room inside The Beverly Hills Hotel, serving American cuisine with an Italian edge since Hollywood's deal-making era.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Polo Lounge Menu Guide (2026) — Prices, What to Order | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to the Polo Lounge at The Beverly Hills Hotel: the $165 Sunday Jazz Brunch, the famous McCarthy salad, signatures, the official dress code, and visiting tips."
  path="/polo-lounge-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/polo-lounge-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/polo-lounge-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of the Polo Lounge's pink-and-green dining room in Beverly Hills"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Beverly Hills
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Polo Lounge — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Inside the Beverly Hills Hotel — the "Pink Palace" that opened in 1912 — the Polo Lounge has
      been the favorite breakfast spot and watering hole for generations of stars and Hollywood
      deal-makers. The pink-and-green dining room serves what the hotel calls American cuisine with
      an Italian edge, and its most famous export is a chopped salad that hasn't changed in
      decades. Below is our independent walkthrough of the menu, the official dress code, and what
      we'd order. Everything is written in our own words; the hotel publishes almost no per-dish
      prices, so we flag exactly where each figure comes from.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">9641 Sunset Blvd, Beverly Hills, CA 90210 (inside The Beverly Hills Hotel)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">American with an Italian edge</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Expensive — the Sunday brunch is $165/person; expect $100+ per person at lunch and dinner</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Accepted online via the official reservation page</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+1 (310) 887-2777</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Breakfast 7–11am · Lunch 11am–3pm · Dinner 5–11pm · Sunday Jazz Brunch 11am–3pm (official site)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Sunday Jazz Brunch — $165 (current)</h2>
      <p>
        This is the one price the hotel publishes outright, and it's current: the Sunday Jazz Brunch
        is a <strong>$165 per person</strong> three-course prix fixe that includes one complimentary
        beverage, served Sundays 11am–3pm with a jazz trio playing on the patio. If you want the full
        Polo Lounge experience with no menu anxiety, this is the booking to make. Prices reported as
        of October 2026, per the hotel's official brunch page.
      </p>

      <h2>Breakfast</h2>
      <p>
        Reported breakfast prices below come from a third-party menu listing dated around
        <strong>January 2025 (dated)</strong> — usable as a rough sense of the range, but likely to
        have moved since.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dish</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Reported price (~Jan 2025, dated)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Classic Cereal with Bananas</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$19.90</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Hollywood Farmers' Market Seasonal Fruit</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$29.80</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Southern California Omelet</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$34.80</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Polo Lounge Avocado Toast</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$35.80</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Green Market Scrambled Eggs</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">$35.80</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Lemon blueberry ricotta pancakes are another reported breakfast signature; their price is
        unverified.
      </p>

      <h2>The McCarthy salad</h2>
      <p>
        The room's signature dish: a chopped salad created in the 1940s and named for polo player
        Neil McCarthy, reportedly unchanged on the menu for decades. A 2020 report put it at about
        <strong>$40 (dated)</strong>; more recent press (December 2024) says the kitchen turns out
        roughly 600 a week. For the hotel's 110th anniversary in December 2024, the Polo Lounge
        offered a <strong>$1,912</strong> gold-leaf anniversary edition — finished with lobster,
        caviar and Dom Pérignon, and served with a take-home Bernardaud bowl. Treat the $40 as a
        dated reference point and confirm the current price when you book.
      </p>

      <h2>Signatures without published prices</h2>
      <p>
        The official site publishes no prices for the rest of the lunch and dinner menu, so we
        describe these without figures — ask when booking rather than trusting old numbers:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Chocolate soufflé</strong> — the famous dessert, arriving on its own little red carpet according to diner reports.</li>
        <li><strong>Dover sole meunière</strong> — the classic tableside-feeling fish preparation.</li>
        <li><strong>"Polo"-branded American Wagyu burger</strong> — the power-lunch burger.</li>
        <li><strong>Chicken tortilla soup</strong> — the California-Italian crossover starter regulars swear by.</li>
        <li><strong>Steak tartare</strong> and <strong>ahi tuna tartare</strong> — the raw-bar pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Old-fashioned chocolate cake</strong> — the other dessert worth knowing about.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Dress code &amp; house rules</h2>
      <p>
        The Polo Lounge publishes an unusually specific dress code (current, from the official site),
        so read it before you go:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Not allowed:</strong> baseball hats, beanies, ripped or shredded denim, crop tops, nightwear, swimwear, men's sleeveless shirts, clothing with offensive messages, flip-flops (Birkenstocks included), and sportswear or tracksuits.</li>
        <li><strong>After 4pm:</strong> no shorts for men; women may wear tailored non-denim shorts.</li>
        <li><strong>Fine:</strong> sweatshirts and hoodies, as long as the hood stays down.</li>
        <li>The code does not apply to children under 12.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Two more house realities: piano accompaniment plays at lunch and dinner daily, and
        photography is frowned upon inside — this is a room built on celebrity discretion, and the
        regulars like it that way.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The non-negotiable:</strong> the McCarthy salad. It's the dish the room is famous for, and it's been made the same way for decades.</li>
        <li><strong>At lunch:</strong> the Wagyu burger or the chicken tortilla soup — the two signatures that feel most like the room.</li>
        <li><strong>On Sunday:</strong> the $165 Jazz Brunch. It's the one price you can plan around, and the patio jazz trio is the experience.</li>
        <li><strong>To finish:</strong> the chocolate soufflé — the red-carpet arrival is half the fun.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book the brunch early</strong> if that's your plan — Sundays 11am–3pm is the headline reservation of the week.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress to the code.</strong> It's specific and enforced; when in doubt, overdress slightly rather than risk the beanie-and-flip-flops rejection.</li>
        <li><strong>Leave the camera in your pocket.</strong> Photography is discouraged, and the room rewards discretion.</li>
        <li><strong>Budget blind spots:</strong> beyond the $165 brunch, per-dish prices aren't published — ask about current prices when you reserve so the bill holds no surprises.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        The <strong>$165 Sunday Jazz Brunch is current</strong> — reported as of October 2026 from
        the hotel's official brunch page. The McCarthy salad's ~$40 figure is from a <strong>2020
        report (dated)</strong>, and the breakfast prices from a third-party listing dated around
        <strong>January 2025 (dated)</strong>. The hotel publishes no other per-dish prices, and we
        do not print figures for dishes we couldn't verify. Always confirm current prices when
        booking.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
